Subject: [PATCH] Fix evaluator bugs, add --repeat for consistency checks (task
 #219)

Prompted by Webb's real live run of task #217's evaluator, 2026-09-01:
38/46 passed, and going through the 8 failures honestly split them
into my own bugs versus real findings.

- scripts/evaluator/runner.py: fix _final_text() -- it short-circuited
  on final_result is None and returned "", instead of calling
  format_for_customer(None), which is itself a meaningful, real reply
  (the "couldn't find that one" no-match message). This produced
  ambiguity-03's false failure: the scenario was actually fine, my own
  helper just never let it see the real text.
- scripts/evaluator/scenarios.py: rewrote two badly-designed scenarios
  that failed for reasons unrelated to what they meant to test.
  ambiguity-02's setup turn named two specific products directly
  rather than browsing a category, so last_presented_products was
  never populated the way the scenario assumed. orders-03's first turn
  ("I want the necklace in 14k") is genuinely ambiguous between a
  price ask and an order ask, unlike orders-01/02's phrasing, which
  both passed live.
- scripts/evaluator/report.py: add print_repeat_summary() -- pass
  count out of N per scenario, PASS/FAIL/FLAKY, one example failure
  detail per distinct check rather than N near-duplicate dumps.
- scripts/run_evaluator.py: add --repeat N, so a flagged scenario can
  be rerun several times with a fresh session each time before
  concluding a failure is a real, repeatable compliance gap rather
  than one unlucky stochastic LLM call -- the exact next step agreed
  with Webb before deciding between prompt reinforcement and a
  deterministic code guard for the ambiguity-compliance findings
  (ambiguity-01, references-02, references-03).
- tests/test_evaluator.py: 3 new tests (the None-handling regression,
  print_repeat_summary's FLAKY/PASS reporting). Full suite: 723
  passed, 29 skipped.

Not done here: actually running --repeat against the real model. Still
needs Webb, no OPENAI_API_KEY in this sandbox.
